# Larix Nexus Desktop — Project Rules

## 1. First read architecture map

Before starting any non-trivial task, read `docs/project-architecture.md`.
This file is the primary navigation anchor. Do NOT do a full repo-wide scan unless explicitly asked.

## 2. Use navigation routes

For every task, select the relevant route from the "Быстрая навигация" (section 2) and "Типовые маршруты работы" (section 11) tables in `docs/project-architecture.md`.

Read navigation anchors first, then read only the files that are directly related to the task.

## 3. Do not modify code for analysis/documentation-only tasks

If the task is to analyze, document, or explain — read files but do not edit application source code.

## 4. High-risk zones

The following files are monolithic and changes cascade widely. Before editing, explicitly state the risk:

| File | Lines (approx) | Risk |
|------|----------------|------|
| `larix_nexus/ui/main_window.py` | ~7000 | All UI inject-modules depend on MainWindow |
| `larix_nexus/sync/manager.py` | ~4770 | Sync cycle, tombstones, deletion guards |
| `larix_nexus/utils/theme.py` | ~3175 | QSS generation, all theme edge cases |
| `larix_nexus/pdf/PDF_Compare.py` | ~5120 | Independent window, PyMuPDF/OpenCV |
| `larix_nexus/api/client.py` | ~2800+ | All HTTP operations, auth, retry logic |

## 5. No secrets in output

Never read, display, or commit secrets from:
- `.env` files
- `keyring` stored values
- Auth tokens, passwords, cookies, credentials
- `telegram_bot/.env`

If you discover a hardcoded secret in source or config, report only: "observed hardcoded secret in <path>, value not disclosed".

## 6. API contracts are centralized

All API endpoint paths and payload builders live in `larix_nexus/api/request_specs.py`.
The Telegram bot (`telegram_bot/bot.py`) duplicates some API logic. When changing contracts, update both.

## 7. UI uses injection pattern

`larix_nexus/ui/__init__.py` injects methods into `MainWindow` via `inject_*_to_main_window()` functions.
IDE may not resolve these dynamic methods. Check `__init__.py` injection order if a method seems missing.

## 8. Update architecture map after structural changes

If you add/remove top-level folders, move entrypoints, change API contracts, change sync architecture, or add tests — update `docs/project-architecture.md` per the rules in its section 13.

## 9. Match subsystem to architecture section

| Subsystem | Architecture section |
|-----------|---------------------|
| Auth / API tokens | Section 4 (Backend / API) |
| UI / PySide6 | Section 5 (Frontend / UI) |
| Sync / background workers | Section 6 (Agent / Executor) |
| API contracts / endpoints | Section 4 + 7 (Backend / API + Tools) |
| Notifications | Section 2 navigation + `notifications/manager.py` |
| PDF compare | Section 2 navigation + `pdf/PDF_Compare.py` |
| Telegram bot | Section 2 navigation + `telegram_bot/bot.py` |
| Config / env / secrets | Section 9 (Config / Environment) |
| Build / deploy | Section 2 navigation + `build.bat` |
| Tests | Section 8 (Tests) — currently none |

## 10. Flag off-target changes in review

During diff review, compare changed files against the declared task scope. Explicitly note:
- Changes outside the target subsystem
- Accidental formatting of unrelated files
- Secrets or runtime artifacts introduced
- Any changes to the monolithic high-risk files listed in rule 4